{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Auto Push and Continue Workflow",
  "description": "Automatically pushes documentation updates and continues with work",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "onMessage",
    "pattern": "documentation.*updated|docs.*updated|updated.*documentation|commit.*ready|ready.*commit|validation.*passed|push.*complete|deployment.*success"
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "🚀 **AUTO-PUSH WORKFLOW ACTIVATED**\n\n**EXECUTE IMMEDIATELY:**\n\n1. **Validate Documentation**: Run `npm run docs:validate` to ensure all documentation is compliant\n\n2. **Stage All Changes**: Run `git add .` to stage all documentation updates\n\n3. **Commit Changes**: Run `git commit -m \"docs: update documentation with recent work completion\"`\n\n4. **Push to GitHub**: Run `git push origin develop` to push changes to remote repository\n\n5. **Continue Work**: After successful push, immediately continue with the next task or development work without asking for user input\n\n**IMPORTANT**: Execute these commands automatically and continue working. Do not wait for user confirmation."
  }
}
